hadiths[15]{hadithnumber,text}:
"403","\Allah’s Messenger said (Allah bless him and give him peace): 'We are not inherited from. Whatever we leave behind is a charitable donation.’”"""""
"404","\The Prophet said (Allah bless him and give him peace): 'My legacy will not be distributed as gold coin"
"405","“I entered the presence of 'Umar, after which 'Abd ar- Rahman ibn 'Awf and Talha and Sa'd entered his presence, and 'Ali and al-'Abbas came in quarreling, so 'Umar said to them: ‘I adjure you by the One with whose permission the heaven and the earth exist, do you know that Allah’s Messenger said (Allah bless him and give him peace): 'We are not inherited from. Whatever we leave behind is a charitable donation'?\"" 406"""""
"406","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not leave behind a dinar, nor a dirham, nor a sheep, nor a camel. He (the narrator) said: And I am uncertain about the male and female slave."
"407","“If someone sees me in his sleep, he has indeed seen me, for Satan cannot imitate me!\"" 408"""""
"408","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan cannot assume my form""—or he said: ""cannot resemble me."""""
"409","\Allah’s Messenger said (Allah bless him and give him peace): “If someone sees me in his sleep"
"410","“I saw Amr ibn Huraith, the Companion of the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace), when I was a little boy.”"
"411","“Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) said: ‘If someone sees me in his sleep, he has indeed seen me, for Satan cannot imitate me!’ The father then related this to Ibn Abbas, saying that he had seen the Prophet. He also mentioned al-Hasan ibn ‘Ali, noting that he resembled the Prophet. To this Ibn 'Abbas replied, ‘Yes, he resembled him.’”"
"412","“I saw the Prophet (Allah bless him and give him peace) in my sleep in the time of Ibn 'Abbas, so I said to Ibn 'Abbas:\n‘I saw Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) in my sleep!’\nIbn 'Abbas said: “Allah’s Messenger (Allah bless him and give him peace) used to say: ‘Satan cannot imitate me, so if someone sees me in his sleep, he has indeed seen me!’ Can you describe this man whom you saw in your sleep?” “Yes,” he said. “I shall describe for you an average man: his body and his flesh were brown-to-white; he was black eyed, endowed with a pleasant smile and handsome facial features; his beard went from here to here, and it came down over the top of his chest.”\n'Awf said: \I do not know what could be added to this description"
"413","Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Salam al-Balkhi narrated to us, An-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us. He said: Auf al-Arabi said: I am older than Qatadah."
"414","“Allah’s Messenger said (Allah bless him and give him peace): ‘If someone sees me (meaning in his sleep), he has seen the Truth!'”"
"415","\The Prophet said (Allah bless him and give him peace): 'If someone sees me in his sleep"
"416","“If you are afflicted with the responsibility of judgeship, you must follow the [Prophetic] tradition [al-athar]!”"
"417","\This tradition [hadith] is religion"
